      "id": "8a969c7d6f3e46619b7a2"
    },
    {
      "text": "####Understanding Aggregation Implementations\ndoing the same thing with groupByKey and reduceByKye\n\n1. reduceByKye: *implementation is much more stable because the reduce happens within each partition and\ndoesn’t need to put everything in memory. Additionally, there is less incurred shuffle during this\noperation; everything happens at each worker individually before performing a final reduce.*\n2. groupByKey:  *each executor must hold all values for a given key in memory\nbefore applying the function to them. Why is this problematic? If you have massive key skew,\nsome partitions might be completely overloaded with a ton of values for a given key, and you\nwill get OutOfMemoryErrors.*\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "d30bad784d1e405eac535"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nfinalflightRdd.map(x => (x(2), x)).groupByKey().map(x => (x._1, x._2.groupBy(x => x(0)))).collect",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "5bbb5629a9574ff19dbb7"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n\nimport scala.util.Random\nval distinctChars = words.flatMap(word => word.toLowerCase.toSeq).distinct\n\nval charRDD = distinctChars.map(c => (c, new Random().nextDouble()))\nval charRDD2 = distinctChars.map(c => (c, new Random().nextDouble()))\nval charRDD3 = distinctChars.map(c => (c, new Random().nextDouble()))\n\ncharRDD.cogroup(charRDD2, charRDD3).take(5)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "8fc528d3762a4c90af4d0"
    },
    {
      "text": "####Join\nRDDs have much the same joins as we saw in the Structured API",
      "config": {
